    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48386" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tingē</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tingi</span></b> , f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of Mauritania</i>, now <i>Tangiers</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 5, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 1, 1,
				§ 4</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tingĭtānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to Tingi</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mamert. Gen. Max. 16 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
